_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.031676680716468245,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":46.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.016260739226642396,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":70.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.089370005,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":59.6,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft, a stock corporation, provides corporate and investment banking, private clients, and asset management products and services in Germany, the United Kingdom, the rest of Europe, the Americas, the Asia-Pacific, the Middle East, and Africa. It operates through Corporate Bank, Investment Bank, Private Bank, and Asset Management segments. The Corporate Bank segment offers cash management services, such as integrated payments and FX solutions; trade finance and lending offerings, including documentary and guarantee business, and structured trade finance and lending; and depository receipts, corporate trust, document custody, and securities services. The Investment Bank segment provides financing solutions in industries and asset classes; institutional sales, trading, and structuring in foreign exchange, rates, emerging markets, and credit trading; liquidity, market making services, and specialized risk management solutions for fixed income and currencies products; and advisory and financial products and services. This segment is also involved in the mergers and acquisitions business; and capital markets businesses in debt and equity. The Private Bank segment offers a range of payment and account services, and credit and deposit products, as well as investment advice, and postal and parcel services; and planning, managing and investing wealth, financing personal and business interests, and servicing institutional and corporate needs. The Asset Management segment provides access to investment capabilities in active and passive asset classes comprising Xtrackers range and alternatives; and access to private equity, private credit, real estate, and infrastructure. Deutsche Bank Aktiengesellschaft was incorporated in 1870 and is headquartered in Frankfurt am Main, Germany.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Christian  Sewing | CEO & Chairman of Management Board | Age 55 | Compensation: $5.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 89K people. Revenue per employee of $386K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers. CEO compensation is 15\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Deutsche Bank AG is a large-cap financial services business with a $67.9B market cap on $34.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield of 3.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.9% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 0/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Deutsche Bank favours Ross Stores and TJX for earnings upside into 2027","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/deutsche-bank-favours-ross-stores-214608191.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794606368.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Pressure Across Staples. Why Deutsche Bank Still Upgraded Unilever (UL)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/pressure-across-staples-why-deutsche-211329314.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604409.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.649,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Flowers Foods Inc (FLO) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Navigating Slower-Than-Expected ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/flowers-foods-inc-flo-q3-230322709.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794611002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Why BofA Calls CoreWeave (CRWV) Funding Needs \u201cManageable\u201d","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/why-bofa-calls-coreweave-crwv-213023720.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794605423.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.599,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GE Aerospace (NYSE:GE) Shares Climb 1.3% 