ear).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.02 across 514 companies in the universe; the top four hold 20% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted lower, down 9% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 12% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 35% and a beta of 1.12, it moves roughly with the market.","About $74.5M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 50% in the 2020 crash, 54% in the 2022 bear market and 83% in 2008."],"val":["On multiples it looks cheap against Financial Services peers: P/E 9.5 vs 12.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 18% above its 10-year median.","The 2 covering analysts target $40.00 on average, 9% above the price."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 10.1%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have been steady (CV 0.20).","Operating margin is running 16pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 7.6% over 3 years and 5.3% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating."],"own":["Insiders own 8.9%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 56%.","It returns 3.2% a year to shareholders (3.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 89,868 employees, each generates about $386K of revenue, 0.8x the Financial Services median, and revenue has grown 2.2% a year across its filed history.","CEO pay is $5.6M (15x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"INSUFFICIENT DATA","conv":null,"head":"Not enough data to value it: missing price or fair value.","pros":[],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":[],"buy_below":null,"vc":null,"med":{"pe":12.2782,"ev_ebitda":10.6105,"pfcf":12.9647,"pb":1.4193,"r